{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/32134-aberrant-updates","id":32134,"title":"Aberrant Updates?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-17T21:02:25-08:00","id":32134,"title":"Aberrant Updates?","content":"So, I have always thought Aberrant had an amazing setting and is still the best super hero style RPG I have ever played. Before I lost my copy, it was used so much that the binding fell a part and I had take all of the pages and put them in a binder.<br /> <br /> I think my biggest issue with it was how Mega Attributes scaled, it got over the top ridiculous and I never let anyone have more then three in my games. <br /> <br /> If and when updates for Aberrant are coming I would like to see a more simplified version of the oWOD rule set and have way better scaled mega attributes like Scion did. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe even figure out a way to use the GMC ruleset on the Aberrant level, but I think a simplified and modified version of what the original Aberrant uses would be great.<br /> <br /> I keep hoping the will put the original books POD, but I have not seen that yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T22:55:28-08:00","id":32181,"title":"","content":"From what we know, the Continuum games, including Aberrant, will be using a new system with a familial connection to the oWOD rules - not necessarily 'simplified', but 'related to'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T02:58:53-08:00","id":33032,"title":"","content":"I hope they keep the new system low-crunch and flowing, one of the nicest things about Aberrant (and Aeon Trinity) was that the system was far less in the way than others of the genre. In Aberrant it was actually possible to do a whole (simple) scenario in one session whereas two of the top superhero RPGs at the time Aberrant came out generally went until the first combat since that would usually take up all the rest of the session time to resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:27:40-08:00","id":33166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/32134-aberrant-updates?p=33032#post33032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they keep the new system low-crunch and flowing</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit of discussion about systems (in the loosest sense with it being early days still), over here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/22290-question-regarding-the-new-trinnity\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-new-trinnity</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T04:45:57-08:00","id":37272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/32134-aberrant-updates?p=33166#post33166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a bit of discussion about systems (in the loosest sense with it being early days still), over here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/22290-question-regarding-the-new-trinnity\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-new-trinnity</a></div> </div> </div> </div>From the thread --<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/22290-question-regarding-the-new-trinnity?p=25294#post25294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The system we're designing for Trinity and Scion is itself a fresh re imagining of the core Storytelling system (at least, it starts from a similar baseline, and the character sheets won't be unrecognizable). It bears little resemblance to Exalted 3e's version of the Storytelling system. Trinity and Scion have a number of needs and concepts in common, and it makes sense for the two to share some base mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/22290-question-regarding-the-new-trinnity?p=26788#post26788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've still got dots, d10 dice pools, and Attributes, but it'll be pretty different in a lot of ways. We can't give out a whole lot of details because it's still being designed.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"http